            <div xml:id="d831">

                <pb facs="1303" n="1289" sameAs="frus:frus1944v01/pg1289"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00116 European War 1939/1344</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        American Representative on the United Nations War Grimes Commission</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Pell</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 8</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-03-18">March 18, 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The receipt is acknowledged of your
                    despatch no. 14144 dated February 29, 1944 concerning the discussion of an
                    international enforcement organization at the meeting of the Committee on Means
                    of Enforcement on February 25. Apparently your despatch and the Department’s
                    instruction no. 6 dated February 15, 1944 crossed in the mails. The instruction
                    referred to summarizes the Department’s tentative views on the subject.</p>
                <p>Very truly yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cordell Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
